Epea (Language Learning API) - License Summary
============================================

Original code in this repository (API, scripts, docs):
  Copyright Jeremiah Lee. License terms for the original code to be
  finalized before publication; until then, all rights reserved.

Language content data (data/epea.db, data/audio):
  Built from the following sources, each recorded with its license and
  attribution text in the database's `sources` table (share_alike=0 for
  all v1 sources - no BY-SA content in v1):

  - Tatoeba (sentence text) - CC BY 2.0 FR. Attribution required.
    https://tatoeba.org
  - Words-CEFR-Dataset (CEFR word levels) - MIT.
    https://github.com/words-cefr/Words-CEFR-Dataset
  - Piper TTS voices (pronunciation audio; voice model license governs
    the generated clips, per the build notes):
      es sharvard (Spanish) - CC BY 3.0
      fr siwis (French) - CC BY 4.0
      it serena (Italian) - CC BY 4.0
      de thorsten (German) - CC0 1.0
      pt cadu (Brazilian Portuguese) - CC0 1.0
      ru denis (Russian) - CC0 1.0
      uk ukrainian_tts (Ukrainian) - CC0 1.0
      nl pim (Dutch) - CC0 1.0
      es-mx ald (Mexican Spanish, opt-in voice) - Unlicense (public domain)
    https://github.com/rhasspy/piper
  - LDNOOBW profanity lists (German, Italian, Portuguese, Dutch,
    Russian) - CC BY 4.0. Attribution required.
    https://github.com/LDNOOBW/List-of-Dirty-Naughty-Obscene-and-Otherwise-Bad-Words
  - Banned-words (Ukrainian) - Apache-2.0.
    https://github.com/readme-SVG/Banned-words

  No Wikipedia/Wikibooks/Wiktionary-derived (BY-SA) content is included
  in v1.

Build-time tools only (never shipped, never in runtime requirements):
  spaCy and its pretrained models, Stanza, Piper, and Torch were used
  solely to generate the database and audio at build time on an isolated
  machine. Their licenses do not govern the generated output; the output
  is covered by the content-source licenses listed above.
